export async function listClassSubjects(classId: number, filters: { status?: "active" | "inactive"; subjectId?: number } = {}) { const db = await getDb(); if (!db) return []; const conditions = [eq(classSubjects.classId, classId)]; if (filters.status) conditions.push(eq(classSubjects.status, filters.status)); if (filters.subjectId) conditions.push(eq(subjects.id, filters.subjectId)); const rows = await db.select({ subject: classSubjects, teacherName: users.name }).from(classSubjects).leftJoin(users, eq(classSubjects.teacherId, users.id)).leftJoin(subjects, eq(subjects.name, classSubjects.name)).where(and(...conditions)).orderBy(asc(classSubjects.displayOrder), asc(classSubjects.name)); return rows.map(row => ({ ...row.subject, teacherName: row.teacherName ?? null })); }
export async function createClassSubject(input: Pick<InsertClassSubject, "classId" | "name" | "arabicName" | "code" | "teacherId" | "subjectType" | "displayOrder">) { const db = await getDb(); if (!db) throw new Error("Database unavailable"); const classRow = await db.select({ id: academyClasses.id }).from(academyClasses).where(and(eq(academyClasses.id, input.classId), eq(academyClasses.status, "active"))).limit(1); if (!classRow[0]) throw new Error("Selected class does not exist or is inactive"); await db.insert(classSubjects).values({ ...input, name: input.name.trim(), arabicName: input.arabicName?.trim() || null, code: input.code?.trim() || null, displayOrder: input.displayOrder ?? 0 }); const created = await db.select().from(classSubjects).where(and(eq(classSubjects.classId, input.classId), eq(classSubjects.name, input.name.trim()))).orderBy(desc(classSubjects.id)).limit(1); return created[0]; }
export async function updateClassSubject(id: number, input: Partial<Pick<InsertClassSubject, "name" | "arabicName" | "code" | "teacherId" | "subjectType" | "displayOrder" | "status">>) { const db = await getDb(); if (!db) throw new Error("Database unavailable"); await db.update(classSubjects).set({ ...input, name: input.name?.trim(), arabicName: input.arabicName?.trim() || null, code: input.code?.trim() || null, updatedAt: new Date() }).where(eq(classSubjects.id, id)); const updated = await db.select().from(classSubjects).where(eq(classSubjects.id, id)).limit(1); return updated[0]; }
export async function deleteClassSubject(id: number) { const db = await getDb(); if (!db) throw new Error("Database unavailable"); await db.delete(classSubjects).where(eq(classSubjects.id, id)); return { id, deleted: true as const }; }

export async function listTeacherWorkload(teacherId?: number) { const db = await getDb(); if (!db) return []; const query = db.select({ assignment: classSubjects, className: academyClasses.name, section: academyClasses.section, teacherName: users.name }).from(classSubjects).innerJoin(academyClasses, eq(classSubjects.classId, academyClasses.id)).leftJoin(users, eq(classSubjects.teacherId, users.id)); let rows; if (teacherId) { const account = await db.select({ id: subjectAccounts.id, subjectId: subjectAccounts.subjectId, linkedSubjectId: users.linkedSubjectId }).from(users).leftJoin(subjectAccounts, eq(subjectAccounts.userId, users.id)).where(eq(users.id, teacherId)).limit(1); const linkedSubjectId = account[0]?.linkedSubjectId ?? account[0]?.subjectId; const subjectAccountId = account[0]?.id; if (linkedSubjectId && subjectAccountId) { const linkedSubject = (await db.select({ name: subjects.name }).from(subjects).where(eq(subjects.id, linkedSubjectId)).limit(1))[0]; const assigned = await db.select({ classId: subjectAccountClasses.classId }).from(subjectAccountClasses).where(eq(subjectAccountClasses.subjectAccountId, subjectAccountId)); rows = linkedSubject && assigned.length ? await query.where(and(eq(classSubjects.name, linkedSubject.name), inArray(classSubjects.classId, assigned.map(item => item.classId)))).orderBy(asc(academyClasses.name), asc(classSubjects.displayOrder), asc(classSubjects.name)) : []; } else rows = await query.where(eq(classSubjects.teacherId, teacherId)).orderBy(asc(academyClasses.name), asc(classSubjects.displayOrder), asc(classSubjects.name)); } else rows = await query.orderBy(asc(users.name), asc(academyClasses.name), asc(classSubjects.displayOrder), asc(classSubjects.name)); return rows.map(row => ({ ...row.assignment, className: row.className, section: row.section, teacherName: row.teacherName ?? "Subject account" })); }

export async function listTeacherPendingResults(teacherId: number) { const db = await getDb(); if (!db) return []; const workload = await listTeacherWorkload(teacherId); const unique = Array.from(new Map(workload.map(item => [`${item.className}::${item.name}`, item])).values()); const summaries = []; for (const item of unique) { const rows = await db.select({ status: resultEntries.status }).from(resultEntries).where(and(eq(resultEntries.className, item.className), eq(resultEntries.subject, item.name))); const draftCount = rows.filter(row => row.status === "draft").length; const submittedCount = rows.filter(row => row.status === "submitted").length; if (draftCount || submittedCount) summaries.push({ className: item.className, section: item.section, subject: item.name, arabicName: item.arabicName ?? null, draftCount, submittedCount, totalCount: rows.length }); } return summaries.sort((a, b) => a.className.localeCompare(b.className) || a.subject.localeCompare(b.subject)); }

